21766413,2026-04-30,Mortgage,Home equity loan or line of credit (HELOC),Closing on a mortgage,Changes in loan terms during or after closing,"I am a contractor operating under XXXX XXXX. My company was engaged by the lender to provide a quote and perform work for a homeowner in connection with a loan being processed.

We were explicitly told by the lender that payment for our work would be issued upon the closing of the loan. Over the course of several weeks, the lender repeatedly stated that the loan was closing imminently and that payment would be released shortly.

Based on these representations, we provided a detailed estimate and committed time and resources in good faith.

We were later informed that the loan had closed. However, despite multiple follow-ups over the following month, we have not received payment. Communication from the lender has been inconsistent, and in many cases ignored, with no clear explanation provided regarding the status of funds.

When we contacted the homeowner directly, she stated that she had been told the contractor would be paid through the loan proceeds. This suggests that funds may have been allocated for this purpose but were not properly disbursed.

Additionally, it appears that our estimate may have been used to support loan underwriting and approval, despite no intention or follow-through to ensure payment for the associated work. If accurate, this raises concerns about the use of contractor documentation in the loan approval process.

As a result : Our company has not been paid for services rendered and time invested The homeowner may be incurring interest on funds that were not properly disbursed for their intended purpose There appears to be a lack of transparency regarding loan fund allocation and contractor payment Requested Resolution : Immediate clarification of loan status and confirmation of whether it has officially closed A full accounting of how loan funds were allocated and disbursed Immediate payment for the contracted scope of work or formal explanation for non-payment Investigation into the lenders practices regarding use of contractor estimates in loan underwriting We are seeking prompt resolution and accountability regarding this matter.",,Nations Mortgage LLC,WI,531XX,,Web,2026-04-30,Closed with explanation,Yes
